---
import ServiceOverviewPage from '@/components/ServiceOverviewPage.astro';

const description = 'Settle IRS or Utah state tax debt with guidance from experienced Utah tax attorneys. Explore affordable resolution options and request a consultation.';
const links = [
  { label: 'Settlement Options', href: '/services/settlement-options/' },
  { label: 'Offer in Compromise', href: '/services/offer-in-compromise-with-utah-tax-attorney/' },
  { label: 'Installment Agreements', href: '/services/installment-agreements/' },
  { label: 'Tax Liens', href: '/services/tax-liens/' },
];
---

<ServiceOverviewPage
  title="Settle Tax Debt in Utah | IRS & State Tax Attorneys"
  description={description}
  heading="Settle Tax Debt Today"
  subheading="We help Utah individuals and businesses resolve IRS and Utah state tax debts."
  eyebrow="Practical Tax Debt Resolution"
  serviceName="IRS and Utah Tax Debt Settlement"
  subject="Tax debt settlement consultation request"
  links={links}
>
  <h2>Utah Tax Settlement Lawyers</h2>
  <p>Our attorneys assist taxpayers who want to settle past tax debt and move forward. The goal is to reach a resolution that is accepted by the taxing authority and realistically affordable for the taxpayer.</p>
  <p>Michelle Turpin, P.C. can explain the different ways to address IRS and Utah tax debts, prepare the required financial disclosures, and communicate with the agency on your behalf. With the right help, many taxpayers can replace uncertainty with a clear resolution plan.</p>
  <h2>Choose a Resolution That Fits the Facts</h2>
  <p>Tax debt cases are not one-size-fits-all. An installment agreement may work for one taxpayer, while another may qualify for an offer in compromise, appeal, penalty relief, or another collection alternative. We review the assessment and collection history before recommending a course of action.</p>
  <h3>Get Help Before Collection Pressure Escalates</h3>
  <p>If you are trying to resolve a tax problem with the IRS or a state taxing authority, contact our office for a confidential consultation. Early action can provide more options and reduce the risk of liens, levies, garnishments, or seizures.</p>
</ServiceOverviewPage>
